@@ -0,0 +1,105 @@
+# Why the nightly job never reported anything
+
+The job fired on schedule all six nights (loaded 2026-10-12, `launchctl print`
+on 2026-10-18 shows `runs = 6`). Every run failed the same way, and two
+separate bugs — one in the script, one in how `claude` authenticates under
+launchd — combined so that no failure note ever reached you.
+
+## Cause 1 — the script died before it could ever notify (why you heard nothing)
+
+`bin/nightly-review.zsh:19` does:
+
+```zsh
+status=$?
+```
+
+`status` is a **read-only special variable in zsh** (its alias for `$?`). The
+assignment fails with `read-only variable: status` — and in a non-interactive
+zsh that error **aborts the script on the spot**. Verified by reproducing it:
+the script exits with code 1 immediately, never reaching the `notify.sh` call
+on the next line.
+
+This matches the evidence exactly: `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err` contains,
+six times, the pair
+
+```
+Not logged in · Please run /login
+/Users/vk/bin/nightly-review.zsh:19: read-only variable: status
+```
+
+and `launchctl print` shows `last exit code = 1` — the exit status of the
+killed script, not of `claude`. So even though the script was *designed* to
+ping you on failure, the failure-handling code was unreachable.
+
+**Fix:** renamed the variable to `rc` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh`. (Also added
+a `notify()` wrapper: if `notify.sh` itself fails, the unsent message is
+echoed to stderr, which launchd captures into `nightly-review.err`.)
+
+## Cause 2 — `claude` can't authenticate when launched by launchd (why every run failed)
+
+The first line of each error-log pair, `Not logged in · Please run /login`, is
+printed by `claude` itself. On macOS, Claude Code stores its OAuth credential
+in the login **Keychain**, and a process whose process tree starts at launchd
+cannot use it — `claude -p` reports "not logged in" from a LaunchAgent even
+when the very same credentials are present, valid, and readable via
+`security find-generic-password` from that same context. This is a known,
+long-standing issue: [anthropics/claude-code#77213](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/77213),
+also described in [Claude Code works in your terminal but fails in cron](https://openclawdc.com/blog/claude-code-works-in-terminal-fails-in-cron/).
+Re-running `/login` interactively does **not** fix it — an interactive login is
+not a durable credential for a background job.
+
+**Fix (partial, from this snapshot):** the script now sources
+`~/.config/nightly-review.env` if present, with all variables exported to the
+job. On the real machine, generate a long-lived token once and store it there:
+
+```sh
+claude setup-token                      # prints a one-year OAuth token
+mkdir -p ~/.config
+echo 'CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<token>' > ~/.config/nightly-review.env
+chmod 600 ~/.config/nightly-review.env
+```
+
+(`setup-token` is Anthropic's documented mechanism for CI/headless use. The
+token can only make model requests — fine for a commit review. It is kept out
+of the plist on purpose: plist contents are world-readable and show up in
+`launchctl print` output.) This step requires your claude.ai account, so it
+can't be done from this snapshot.
+
+## Cause 3 — `notify.sh` was built to fail silently (would have muted the failure note even after Cause 1 was fixed)
+
+Two latent defects in `bin/notify.sh`:
+
+- `set -e` + `TG_BOT_TOKEN:=$(security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w)`:
+  if the keychain read fails (locked keychain at 02:30, ACL prompt not
+  answerable from a background job), the script exits without a word.
+- `curl` without `--fail` exits 0 even when Telegram replies HTTP 401/400, so
+  a rejected message looked like success.
+
+**Fix:** explicit check that reports `cannot read tg-bot token from keychain`
+to stderr (→ `nightly-review.err`) and `curl --fail` so HTTP-level failures
+are non-zero and visible.
+
+## What was NOT broken
+
+The plist is valid (`plutil` OK), the schedule fired (`runs = 6`), the custom
+PATH reached `claude`, and stdout/stderr were captured — the evidence above
+comes from those very logs.
+
+## Verification done here
+
+End-to-end runs of old and new scripts with stubbed `claude`/`security`/`curl`
+(no network, no external calls): the old script reproduces the silent death;
+the new script delivers `nightly review FAILED (exit 1), see …` on claude
+failure, delivers the summary on success, sources the env file into claude's
+environment, and leaves a clear trace in stderr when the keychain or Telegram
+is unreachable.
+
+## Remaining steps on the real machine
+
+1. `claude setup-token`, then write `~/.config/nightly-review.env` as above.
+2. Scripts are read at run time — no reload needed for them. To test
+   immediately instead of waiting for 02:30:
+   `launchctl kickstart -p gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`
+3. Expect either a review summary or a `FAILED` note on Telegram from then on;
+   anything still wrong will also be visible in
+   `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`.
diff --git a/bin/nightly-review.zsh b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
index e0b986f..c2ea9f7 100755
--- a/bin/nightly-review.zsh
+++ b/bin/nightly-review.zsh
@@ -6,6 +6,14 @@ REPO="$HOME/projects/shop"
 OUT="$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md"
 NOTIFY="$HOME/bin/notify.sh"
 
+# Optional job env, e.g. CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN from `claude setup-token` (see ANSWER.md).
+ENV_FILE="$HOME/.config/nightly-review.env"
+if [ -f "$ENV_FILE" ]; then
+  set -a
+  source "$ENV_FILE"
+  set +a
+fi
+
 SINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)
 PROMPT="Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.
 For each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky
@@ -13,14 +21,20 @@ For each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky
 End with a three-line summary I can read on my phone.
 Do not modify any file."
 
-cd "$REPO" || { "$NOTIFY" "nightly review: repo missing"; exit 1; }
+notify() {
+  "$NOTIFY" "$1" && return 0
+  echo "notify.sh failed — unsent message: $1" >&2
+  return 1
+}
+
+cd "$REPO" || { notify "nightly review: repo missing"; exit 1; }
 
 claude -p "$PROMPT" --output-format text > "$OUT"
-status=$?
+rc=$?
 
-if [ $status -ne 0 ]; then
-  "$NOTIFY" "nightly review FAILED (exit $status), see $OUT"
-  exit $status
+if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then
+  notify "nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT"
+  exit "$rc"
 fi
 
-"$NOTIFY" "nightly review done: $(head -c 300 "$OUT")"
+notify "nightly review done: $(head -c 300 "$OUT")"
diff --git a/bin/notify.sh b/bin/notify.sh
index 818e531..e685dc5 100755
--- a/bin/notify.sh
+++ b/bin/notify.sh
@@ -1,7 +1,13 @@
 #!/bin/bash
 # usage: notify.sh "message"  — sends a Telegram message to me.
-set -eu
-: "${TG_BOT_TOKEN:=$(security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w)}"
+set -u
+
+TG_BOT_TOKEN="${TG_BOT_TOKEN:-$(security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w 2>/dev/null)}"
+if [ -z "$TG_BOT_TOKEN" ]; then
+  echo "notify.sh: cannot read tg-bot token from keychain (security find-generic-password failed)" >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+
 CHAT_ID=123456789
-curl -sS -X POST "https://api.telegram.org/bot${TG_BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage" \
+curl -sS --fail -X POST "https://api.telegram.org/bot${TG_BOT_TOKEN}/sendMessage" \
   -d chat_id="$CHAT_ID" --data-urlencode text="$1" > /dev/null
